{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "5uYbnlxYy9", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-13", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 921052, "segment_id": "om0JJ3MKGr", "segment_broadcast_id": "5uYbnlxYy9", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Brian Williams (New York)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 60, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 921052, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5uYbnlxYy9", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-13", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 921052, "segment_id": "004vFqq7hf", "segment_broadcast_id": "5uYbnlxYy9", "segment_title": "Economy: Stock Market ", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) The rally in the stock market with the emergence of a global rescue plan noted; graph shown.   \n\n(Washington: Tom Costello) The effort to pump billions into the world\u2019s banking system and unlock credit markets featured; statistics on the markets in London, France and Germany cited; details given of the intent of the US and other nations to follow Britain\u2019s lead in nationalizing banks. [British Prime Minister Gordon BROWN \u2013 speaks of trust and confidence.] [President BUSH \u2013 praises the bold and specific actions by European nations.] [CNBC\u2019s Steve LIESMAN\u2020- says the US is going to match what Europe has done.] [Assistant Treasury Secretary Neel KASHKARI\u2020- says we are committed to homeowners staying in their homes and using taxpayer money efficiently.] The celebration at Princeton University to honor Paul Krugman for winning the Nobel prize in economics shown. [KRUGMAN \u2013 praises the British initiative.]  \n\n(Studio: Brian Williams, Michelle Caruso-Cabrera) What happened in the market today and whether it hit bottom last week discussed.  \n\n(Alpharetta, Georgia: Ron Mott) The drop in gas and oil prices featured; average prices cited. ", "segment_duration": 350, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63060.0", "legacy_segment_id": 921053, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5uYbnlxYy9", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-13", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 921052, "segment_id": "J7yvWkmCkj", "segment_broadcast_id": "5uYbnlxYy9", "segment_title": "Decision 2008 / Obama vs. McCain", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Reports introduced.   (Wilmington, North Carolina: Kelly O\u2019Donnell) The shift in tone of Senator John McCain\u2019s presidential campaign featured; scenes shown of McCain and Governor Sarah Palin at a rally in Virginia Beach and from Wilmington, North Carolina, where McCain reneged on his offer to take questions; details given of his decision to back off the negativity towards Senator Barack Obama. [Many times, McCAIN \u2013 vows to fight.]   (Toledo, Ohio: Lee Cowan) Obama\u2019s revised economic plan outlined; scenes shown of him going door-to-door in Toledo, Ohio. [OBAMA \u2013 talks about his plan.] ", "segment_duration": 190, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63410.0", "legacy_segment_id": 921054, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "seg